        "bytes": 3159
      },
      "exactReplacement": {
        "before": "The same cap applies if the case a=1 relative to F is lost solely through invalid division by a-1 and is not handled correctly anywhere else: the central change from an intersection line to an entire plane has then not been investigated. A correct treatment of the exceptional case elsewhere counts.",
        "after": "The same cap applies if no mathematically sound treatment of the exceptional case a=1 relative to F is evident anywhere in the submission. The change from an intersection line for a≠1 to the entire plane for a=1 must not be entirely absent. This includes simply omitting the case as well as losing it through invalid division by a−1. A concise justified statement that E₁=F is sufficient; a correct treatment elsewhere counts. A single local arithmetic or copying error alone still does not trigger the cap."
      },
